    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "Catherine is $\\frac{5}{6}$ of her father’s height and her brother Peter is $\\frac{7}{9}$ of their father’s height. If Peter is 140 cm tall, how tall is Catherine?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$150\\text{ cm}$",
      "worked": "Father’s height:\n$$\\begin{align*}140\\div\\frac{7}{9}&=140\\times\\frac{9}{7}\\\\140\\div\\frac{7}{9}&=180\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nCatherine’s height:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5}{6}\\times180&=5\\times30\\\\\\frac{5}{6}\\times180&=150\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
